<title>USA: Individual investments hurt 1996 results.</title>
<headline>Individual investments hurt 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Individual Investor Group Inc on Monday said that certain investments made in 1996 contributed to the firms reported net year loss and will likely remain a constraint to profits through the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>The investments were in advertising, sales, personnel, marketing and promotional efforts. The firm did not give financial details for the investments.</p>
<p>Earlier, the company said it posted a loss of $3.19 million, or $0.51 per share, compared with net income of $2.89 million, or $0.49 per share, in 1995.</p>
